      "number": 27712,
      "title": "feat(lexer): add types for runtime feature detection",
      "url": "https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/pull/27712",
      "author": "overlookmotel",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-17T13:28:38Z",
      "labels": [
        "A-lexer"
      ],
      "hint": "feature",
      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "This PR is the start of the transition from compile-time CPU features detection to runtime detection.\n\nIt introduces:\n\n- `DynCpu`: Enum representing any of the CPU feature sets available on the current platform.\n- `Avx2`, `Neon`, `Generic`: Zero-sized types which each represent a single CPU feature set.\n- `Cpu`: Trait which is implemented for all the above types.\n- `cpu_select!`: Macro to dispatch to a different implementation depending on CPU capabilities, given an `impl Cpu`.\n- `cpu_versions!`: Macro to generate multiple versions of a function for all CPU feature sets available on current platform, with an entry point that dispatches to the appropriate one depending on what `impl Cpu` is passed to it.\n\n`DynCpu` and the feature set types (`Avx2`, `Neon`, `Generic`) are unforgeable. `DynCpu` can only be created with `DynCpu::detect()`, which returns a definitive answer. `Avx2` etc types can only be obtained from `DynCpu`, so they act as tokens guaranteeing that feature set _is_ supported on current CPU.\n\nTherefore, it's statically impossible to call a function which takes `Avx2` as a parameter when the CPU does not support AVX2. This invariant is a type system-level guarantee, meaning that some functions which would otherwise be unsafe purely because they rely on a specific CPU feature set can become safe functions.\n\nThis PR only introduces these primitives, it does not use them anywhere in `oxc_lexer` yet. Migrating over to them can happen incrementally. Later PRs in this st\n…(truncated)",
      "files": [
        "Cargo.lock (+7 -0)",
        "Cargo.toml (+1 -0)",
        "crates/oxc_lexer/Cargo.toml (+1 -0)",
        "crates/oxc_lexer/src/pipeline/cpu.rs (+953 -0)",
        "crates/oxc_lexer/src/pipeline/mod.rs (+1 -0)"
      ],
      "filesTotal": 5
    },
